636
00:29:14,840 --> 00:29:16,840
The other aspect of Kahneman-Tversky

637
00:29:16,840 --> 00:29:18,840
is the weighting function.

638
00:29:18,840 --> 00:29:19,840
Okay.

639
00:29:19,840 --> 00:29:26,840
And I'm going to draw, again, a picture of it.

640
00:29:26,840 --> 00:29:31,840
And it's this time, it's how people psychologically

641
00:29:31,840 --> 00:29:33,840
think about probabilities.

642
00:29:33,840 --> 00:29:38,840
And this, again, is Kahneman-Tversky.

643
00:29:38,840 --> 00:29:41,840
A probability is a number between 0 and 1,

644
00:29:41,840 --> 00:29:43,840
or 0 and 100%.

645
00:29:43,840 --> 00:29:47,840
I'll put 0 here and 1 here.

646
00:29:47,840 --> 00:29:50,840
We can tell someone the probability of something,

647
00:29:50,840 --> 00:29:53,840
but they can't accept it psychologically.

648
00:29:53,840 --> 00:29:56,840
The errors that people make

649
00:29:56,840 --> 00:29:58,840
are described by the weighting function.

650
00:29:58,840 --> 00:30:00,840
What the weighting function is,

651
00:30:00,840 --> 00:30:02,840
the psychological impact.

652
00:30:02,840 --> 00:30:06,840
You are behaving as if you don't understand the probability.

653
00:30:06,840 --> 00:30:08,840
So, what Kahneman-Tversky say

654
00:30:08,840 --> 00:30:12,840
is that for very low probabilities,

655
00:30:12,840 --> 00:30:15,840
people may round them to 0.

656
00:30:15,840 --> 00:30:17,840
And for very high probabilities,

657
00:30:17,840 --> 00:30:19,840
they may round them to 1.

658
00:30:19,840 --> 00:30:21,840
But if they decide not to

659
00:30:21,840 --> 00:30:23,840
round them to 0 or 1,

660
00:30:23,840 --> 00:30:27,840
they exaggerate the difference between 0 and 1.

661
00:30:27,840 --> 00:30:29,840
You just can't think in

662
00:30:29,840 --> 00:30:31,840
terms of a continuum of probabilities.

663
00:30:31,840 --> 00:30:33,840
So, this is what the weighting function,

664
00:30:33,840 --> 00:30:36,840
this is the weight as a function of the probability.

665
00:30:36,840 --> 00:30:39,840
For low probabilities, it's 0.

666
00:30:39,840 --> 00:30:41,840
I'm going to maybe exaggerate it here.

667
00:30:41,840 --> 00:30:43,840
Then it jumps up.

668
00:30:43,840 --> 00:30:44,840
And it's something like,

669
00:30:44,840 --> 00:30:46,840
it's something like this.

670
00:30:46,840 --> 00:30:48,840
And as it gets close to 1,

671
00:30:48,840 --> 00:30:51,840
it jumps up to 1 again.

672
00:30:51,840 --> 00:30:54,840
So, you see, it's like a broken line segment.

673
00:30:54,840 --> 00:30:56,840
And there's been various versions of this theory,

674
00:30:56,840 --> 00:31:00,840
but this is the simplest version of it.

675
00:31:00,840 --> 00:31:01,840
So, that means,

676
00:31:01,840 --> 00:31:03,840
if you're getting on an airplane,

677
00:31:03,840 --> 00:31:06,840
you think, well, what's the probability

678
00:31:06,840 --> 00:31:08,840
of this airplane crashing?

679
00:31:08,840 --> 00:31:10,840
Well, you know, it's probably something like

680
00:31:10,840 --> 00:31:13,840
1 in 10 million or even less than that.

681
00:31:13,840 --> 00:31:14,840
So, what's the probability

682
00:31:14,840 --> 00:31:15,840
of this plane crashing?

683
00:31:15,840 --> 00:31:17,840
Well, most of us in our mind just say,

684
00:31:17,840 --> 00:31:18,840
it's 0 and I'm done.

685
00:31:18,840 --> 00:31:19,840
I'm not going to think about it.

686
00:31:19,840 --> 00:31:21,840
I'm not going to worry about it.

687
00:31:21,840 --> 00:31:22,840
And so, we're down here.

688
00:31:22,840 --> 00:31:24,840
We've rounded it to 0.

689
00:31:24,840 --> 00:31:27,840
But some people don't round it to 0, okay?

690
00:31:27,840 --> 00:31:29,340
And for them, they just

691
00:31:29,340 --> 00:31:30,840
blow it out of all proportion

692
00:31:30,840 --> 00:31:33,840
in their minds and it becomes exaggerated.

693
00:31:33,840 --> 00:31:34,840
So, I have it here.

694
00:31:34,840 --> 00:31:36,840
So, it looks like it's a half.

695
00:31:36,840 --> 00:31:40,840
So, this would be 1 here.

696
00:31:40,840 --> 00:31:42,840
And this is about 0.4.

697
00:31:42,840 --> 00:31:43,840
And then, ultimately,

698
00:31:43,840 --> 00:31:45,840
if the probability gets really high,

699
00:31:45,840 --> 00:31:47,840
then I'm not even going to think about it.

700
00:31:47,840 --> 00:31:49,840
It's 1, okay?

701
00:31:49,840 --> 00:31:51,840
So, you know, it's a little bit like people,

702
00:31:51,840 --> 00:31:54,840
in some of the most primitive languages in the world,

703
00:31:54,840 --> 00:31:57,840
there's only a couple of numbers.

704
00:31:57,840 --> 00:31:59,840
There's 0, there's 1,

705
00:31:59,840 --> 00:32:01,840
maybe there's 2 or 3,

706
00:32:01,840 --> 00:32:03,840
and then there's no more numbers.

707
00:32:03,840 --> 00:32:05,840
But our minds are still very primitive

708
00:32:05,840 --> 00:32:07,840
in dealing with probabilities.

